= The Left: advisers

The Left is the party of Berlin, Hamburg and the Ruhr, impatient for the offensive: Fischer who agitates, Maslow who organises, Thälmann who drills the Hamburg fighters, Scholem who writes against the SPD leaders. Each can act once every three months. A faction that is not consulted for six months while it still has real strength grows angry.

- @fischer
- @maslow
- @thaelmann
- @scholem
- @root: Return to main

@fischer
title: Ruth Fischer: mobilise Berlin
subtitle: dev: kf_left_strength +6, kf_right_dissent +4, adv_left_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if fischer_timer > 0 : [+ fischer_timer +] months before Fischer can act again. ?]
choose-if: fischer_timer = 0
on-arrival: fischer_timer = 3; kf_left_strength += 6; kf_right_dissent += 4; adv_left_last = time

Fischer fills the Berlin halls and speaks for the offensive. The crowds are loud and the Left grows. The Right asks quietly what the party is doing with all that noise.

@maslow
title: Arkadi Maslow: organise the districts
subtitle: dev: kf_left_dissent −5, kf_left_strength +3, adv_left_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if maslow_timer > 0 : [+ maslow_timer +] months before Maslow can act again. ?]
choose-if: maslow_timer = 0
on-arrival: maslow_timer = 3; kf_left_dissent -= 5; kf_left_strength += 3; adv_left_last = time

Maslow organises the Left in the districts where Berlin has never been listened to, and gives them tasks. A Left with something to do is quieter than a Left with nothing.

@thaelmann
title: Ernst Thälmann: train the Hamburg fighters
subtitle: dev: rfb_strength +15, kf_left_strength +3, adv_left_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if thaelmann_timer > 0 : [+ thaelmann_timer +] months before Thälmann can act again. ?]
choose-if: thaelmann_timer = 0
on-arrival: thaelmann_timer = 3; rfb_strength += 15; kf_left_strength += 3; adv_left_last = time

Thälmann's Hamburg organisation grows. The defence units drill, and the police take note.

@scholem
title: Werner Scholem: write against the SPD leaders
subtitle: dev: kf_left_strength +4, workers_spd −2, kf_right_dissent +2, adv_left_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if scholem_timer > 0 : [+ scholem_timer +] months before Scholem can act again. ?]
choose-if: scholem_timer = 0
on-arrival: scholem_timer = 3; kf_left_strength += 4; workers_spd -= 2; kf_right_dissent += 2; adv_left_last = time

Scholem writes the party's case against the SPD leaders, as sharply as he can. Some SPD workers are won over and many are offended, and the majority, which would like to keep the united front, flinches.
